Comparable interface
The Comparable Interface in Java is used to define the natural sorting order of objects.
For example, if you want to sort Student objects by their id, name, or marks, you use the Comparable interface.
Syntax
public class Student implements Comparable<Student> {
    @Override
    public int compareTo(Student s) {
        // comparison logic
    }
}
Why do we use Comparable?
Normally, Java knows how to sort primitive wrapper classes like:
Integer
String
Double
Character
