Stream Api
Stream API is a Java 8 feature used to process collections (like ArrayList, List, Set) in a simple and efficient way.
Intermediate Operations
filter()
map()
sorted()
distinct()
limit()
skip()

Example
import java.util.*;

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(10,20,30,40,50);

        list.stream()
            .filter(n -> n > 20);
    }
}
Output
No Output
Why?
Because
.filter()
is only an Intermediate Operation.
It prepares the stream but doesn't execute it.
Terminal Operation
Terminal operation starts the execution of the stream and produces the final result.
Terminal Methods
forEach()
collect()
count()
reduce()
findFirst()
findAny()
min()
max()
filter()	Condition apply 
map()	Value change 
sorted()	Sort 
count()	Count 
limit()	First n values 
distinct()	Duplicate remove 
forEach()	Print or process 
