Optional class 
Optional is a container object introduced in Java 8 that may contain a non-null value or may be empty. It is mainly used to avoid NullPointerException and write cleaner code.
Method	Purpose
of(value)	Creates an Optional with a non-null value
ofNullable(value)	Accepts both null and non-null values
empty()	Creates an empty Optional
isPresent()	Checks if a value exists
get()	Returns the value (throws if empty)
orElse(default)	Returns the value or a default
orElseThrow()	Throws an exception if empty
ifPresent()	Executes code if a value is present
Why was Optional introduced?

Before Java 8, suppose we have:

String name = null;

System.out.println(name.length());
Output
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.NullPointerException
Example

Imagine a gift box 🎁.

Box contains a gift
+------------+
|  Chocolate |
+------------+

Optional = Box

Value = Chocolate

Empty Box
+------------+
|   Empty    |
+------------+

No error.

Just empty.

